  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather through this weekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nVery quiet weather persists through the weekend. There is a \nstrong low pressure system off the Mid-Atlantic that will track \nnortheast through Thursday night, but it will pass well to our \nsoutheast and not bring any precipitation to our area except\nperhaps over our outer waters. We will also have a cold front \nmoving through from north to south late tonight into Thursday, \nbut there will not be any precipitation with the front, and just\nsome increased cloudcover. The main change we will see is \nincreased winds during the day Thursday, Thursday night, and \ninto Friday. Gusts up to about 30 mph from the north are \nexpected during the day Thursday and Friday, which will not be \nenough for any impacts to trees and power, though additional \nleaf loss is expected. As high pressure builds in Friday night,\ntemperatures will dip into the 20s areawide, with even a few\nteens possible in the colder valleys in north/northwest areas.\nExtremely quiet weather for the weekend, with a warming trend\ninto Sunday. The next small chance of rain comes Monday, but it\nis not looking impressive, as it looks like another moisture- \nstarved cold front moving in from the north.",
